ssiah, Shiloh, Christ, Jesus Christ, Messias","summary":"Anointed, the Greek translation of the Hebrew word rendered “Messiah”, the official title of our Lord, occurring five hundred and fourteen times in the New Testament.","verses":1831,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[1,3,5,6,8,9,16,20,23,25]},{"id":"paul_2479","name":"Paul","also":"Saul, Mercurius","summary":"Saul was born about the same time as our Lord. His circumcision-name was Saul, and probably the name Paul was also given to him in infancy “for use in the Gentile world,” as “Saul” would be his Hebrew home-name.","verses":179,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,9,19]},{"id":"timotheus_2863","name":"Timotheus","also":"Timothy","summary":"Honouring God, a young disciple who was Paul’s companion in many of his journeyings. His mother, Eunice, and his grandmother, Lois, are mentioned as eminent for their piety (2 Tim. 1:5).","verses":24,"father":"","mother":"Eunice","v":[1]},{"id":"philemon_2342","name":"Philemon","also":"","summary":"An inhabitant of Colosse, and apparently a person of some note among the citizens (Col. 4:9; Philemon 1:2). He was brought to a knowledge of the gospel through the instrumentality of Paul (19), and held a prominent place in the Christian community for his piety and beneficence (4-7).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"archippus_292","name":"Archippus","also":"","summary":"Master of the horse, a “fellow-soldier” of Paul’s (Philemon 1:2), whom he exhorts to renewed activity (Col. 4:17).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"apphia_278","name":"Apphia","also":"","summary":"Increasing, a female Christian at Colosse (Philemon 1:2), supposed by some to have been the wife of Philemon.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"onesimus_2251","name":"Onesimus","also":"","summary":"Useful, a slave who, after robbing his master Philemon at Colosse, fled to Rome, where he was converted by the apostle Paul, who sent him back to his master with the epistle which bears his name.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"epaphras_1195","name":"Epaphras","also":"","summary":"Lovely, spoken of by Paul (Col. 1:7; 4:12) as “his dear fellow-servant,” and “a faithful minister of Christ.” He was thus evidently with him at Rome when he wrote to the Colossians.","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[23]},{"id":"mark_1679","name":"John","also":"Marcus","summary":"The evangelist; “John whose surname was Mark” (Acts 12:12, 25). Mark (Marcus, Col. 4:10, etc.) was his Roman name, which gradually came to supersede his Jewish name John.","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"Mary","v":[24]},{"id":"aristarchus_306","name":"Aristarchus","also":"","summary":"Best ruler, native of Thessalonica (Acts 20:4), a companion of Paul (Acts 19:29; 27:2).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"demas_1006","name":"Demas","also":"","summary":"A companion and fellow-labourer of Paul during his first imprisonment at Rome (Philemon 1:24; Col. 4:14).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"luke_1836","name":"Luke","also":"Lucas","summary":"The evangelist, was a Gentile. The date and circumstances of his conversion are unknown. According to his own statement (Luke 1:2), he was not an “eye-witness and minister of the word from the beginning.”","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[24]}],"places":[],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3972,1198,1198,5547,5547,2424,2532,5095,3588,80,5371,5371,1473,27,4904,4904],[682,682,3588,79,751,751,1473,4961,4961,2532,3588,3588,1577,2596,2596,2596,4771,3624],[5485,2532,1515,4771,4771,575,2316,1473,3962,2532,2962,2962,2424,5547],[2168,2168,2168,1473,2316,4160,4771,1909,1473,4335],[191,191,191,191,2192,4102,4314,3588,2962,2424,2532,4771,26,1519,3956,3588,40],[3704,3704,3704,4771,2842,3588,3588,4102,1096,1096,1756,1722,1922,1922,1922,3956,18,18,3588,3588,1473,1519,5547],[2192,2192,4183,5479,2532,3874,1909,4771,26,3754,4771,80,373,373,3588,469